@cc [owner:fabiencelier,label:error-handling] encoders-throw-invalid-input
Exception to `no-catching-own-errors`: the `encode*` functions of `codec.ts` MUST throw
`DfsError("invalid_input")` for inputs that cannot be represented on the wire (malformed object ids,
values outside their protobuf integer type) instead of returning them as `Err`, and MUST NOT throw any
other `DfsError`. Only `DfsClient` request building MAY catch them, using an `instanceof DfsError`
guard and rethrowing anything else.
